  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 236 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nPrecipitation more robust than earlier anticipated with outflow and \nMCV from convection to the northwest combining with warm-air \nadvection ahead of these features. Some brief strong updrafts have \noccurred but limited instability and modest focusing mechanisms \nkeeping impacts low. This activity should slowly push off this \nmorning with some recovery of temperatures in the afternoon though \npassage of a weak front should keep heat indicies below Advisory \nlevel. \n\nUpper flow becomes weak northwesterly around the weaker upper high \nto the southwest bringing occasional chances for high-based showers \nand thunderstorms over the next few days as models keep the mid-\nlevels moist. The main windows for this appear to be late tonight \ninto Wednesday morning then again Wednesday night into early \nThursday. Continuity remains in a shortwave trough diving southeast \nacross the mid-Mississippi Valley late Thursday into Friday for mid-\nrange precip chances locally. Instability and shear still look weak\nbut precipitable water values look to be around 2 inches into late \nWednesday and bump up a bit more into Thursday for some concern for \nlocally heavy rainfall, but again lacking any focusing mechanism this\npotential is low. More northerly upper flow takes hold this weekend \nwith modified high pressure bringing in drier and cooler air for \nbenign conditions.",
